rprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","02.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":234,"title":224,"body":235,"description":737,"extension":738,"links":739,"meta":740,"navigation":741,"path":225,"seo":742,"stem":226,"__hash__":743},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security.md",{"type":236,"value":237,"toc":721},"minimark",[238,242,255,260,320,324,328,422,426,483,487,547,551,586,590,636,640],[239,240,25],"h2",{"id":241},"overview",[243,244,245,246,250,251,254],"p",{},"Every Kinotic service image is inventoried and scanned for known vulnerabilities before it is published. An image with a Critical vulnerability that has a published fix is never promoted to Docker Hub. Every control on this page runs automatically in the ",[247,248,249],"code",{},"Build and Publish"," workflow (",[247,252,253],{},".github\u002Fworkflows\u002Fgradle-build.yml","), and each one leaves evidence in GitHub.",[256,257,259],"h3",{"id":258},"scope","Scope",[261,262,263,276],"table",{},[264,265,266],"thead",{},[267,268,269,273],"tr",{},[270,271,272],"th",{},"Image",[270,274,275],{},"Published as",[277,278,279,290,300,310],"tbody",{},[267,280,281,285],{},[282,283,284],"td",{},"Kinotic management server",[282,286,287],{},[247,288,289],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-server-management",[267,291,292,295],{},[282,293,294],{},"Kinotic system server",[282,296,297],{},[247,298,299],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-server-system",[267,301,302,305],{},[282,303,304],{},"Kinotic app server",[282,306,307],{},[247,308,309],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-server-app",[267,311,312,315],{},[282,313,314],{},"Kinotic migration",[282,316,317],{},[247,318,319],{},"kinoticai\u002Fkinotic-migration",[239,321,323],{"id":322},"controls","Controls",[256,325,327],{"id":326},"software-inventory-sbom","Software inventory (SBOM)",[261,329,330,338],{},[264,331,332],{},[267,333,334,336],{},[270,335],{},[270,337],{},[277,339,340,351,369,387,412],{},[267,341,342,348],{},[282,343,344],{},[345,346,347],"strong",{},"Control",[282,349,350],{},"Each build produces a software bill of materials for each image. It lists every operating-system package and application library in the image, with its version.",[267,352,353,358],{},[282,354,355],{},[345,356,357],{},"Format",[282,359,360,361,368],{},"CycloneDX JSON, generated with ",[362,363,367],"a",{"href":364,"rel":365},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fanchore\u002Fsyft",[366],"nofollow","Syft"," from the built image, not from source manifests. The inventory therefore matches what runs.",[267,370,371,376],{},[282,372,373],{},[345,374,375],{},"Frequency",[282,377,378,379,382,383,386],{},"Every build of the images: each pull request into ",[247,380,381],{},"develop"," or ",[247,384,385],{},"main",", each push to them that changes application code, and nightly.",[267,388,389,394],{},[282,390,391],{},[345,392,393],{},"Evidence",[282,395,396,397,400,401,400,404,407,408,411],{},"Workflow run artifacts named ",[247,398,399],{},"sbom-kinotic-server-management.cdx.json",", ",[247,402,403],{},"sbom-kinotic-server-system.cdx.json",[247,405,406],{},"sbom-kinotic-server-app.cdx.json"," and ",[247,409,410],{},"sbom-kinotic-migration.cdx.json",".",[267,413,414,419],{},[282,415,416],{},[345,417,418],{},"Retention",[282,420,421],{},"90 days.",[256,423,425],{"id":424},"vulnerability-scanning","Vulnerability scanning",[261,427,428,436],{},[264,429,430],{},[267,431,432,434],{},[270,433],{},[270,435],{},[277,437,438,452,461],{},[267,439,440,444],{},[282,441,442],{},[345,443,347],{},[282,445,446,451],{},[362,447,450],{"href":448,"rel":449},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fanchore\u002Fgrype",[366],"Grype"," scans each image's SBOM against current vulnerability advisories: GitHub Security Advisories, the National Vulnerability Database, and operating-system vendor feeds. The scan covers the same artifact the inventory records.",[267,453,454,458],{},[282,455,456],{},[345,457,375],{},[282,459,460],{},"Every build, including each pull request, and nightly. The nightly run checks newly published advisories against the current images.",[267,462,463,467],{},[282,464,465],{},[345,466,393],{},[282,468,469,470,400,473,400,476,407,479,482],{},"Findings of every severity are recorded as GitHub code scanning alerts in the categories ",[247,471,472],{},"image-kinotic-server-management",[247,474,475],{},"image-kinotic-server-system",[247,477,478],{},"image-kinotic-server-app",[247,480,481],{},"image-kinotic-migration",", with open and fixed history per finding. Each workflow run's summary lists the fixable findings for each image.",[256,484,486],{"id":485},"release-gate","Release gate",[261,488,489,497],{},[264,490,491],{},[267,492,493,495],{},[270,494],{},[270,496],{},[277,498,499,517,527],{},[267,500,501,505],{},[282,502,503],{},[345,504,347],{},[282,506,507,508,511,512,382,514,516],{},"A build fails when either image has a ",[345,509,510],{},"Critical"," vulnerability with a published fix. On a pull request, the failure is reported on the change before it merges. Only an image from a fully passing build of ",[247,513,381],{},[247,515,385],{}," is promoted from the staging registry (ghcr.io) to Docker Hub.",[267,518,519,524],{},[282,520,521],{},[345,522,523],{},"Effect",[282,525,526],{},"An image is published only when, at build time, it has no known Critical vulnerability with an available fix.",[267,528,529,533],{},[282,530,531],{},[345,532,393],{},[282,534,535,536,539,540,543,544,546],{},"The ",[247,537,538],{},"SBOM and Vulnerability Scan"," jobs and the ",[247,541,542],{},"Build Result"," job of each workflow run. ",[247,545,542],{}," performs the promotion and records which job withheld it.",[256,548,550],{"id":549},"integrity-of-the-scanning-tools","Integrity of the scanning tools",[261,552,553,561],{},[264,554,555],{},[267,556,557,559],{},[270,558],{},[270,560],{},[277,562,563,572],{},[267,564,565,569],{},[282,566,567],{},[345,568,347],{},[282,570,571],{},"Third-party actions in the scan job are pinned to full commit SHAs rather than version tags, so a repointed tag cannot change the code that runs. The scan job has read-only access to repository contents and holds no publishing, signing or deployment credentials.",[267,573,574,579],{},[282,575,576],{},[345,577,578],{},"Maintenance",[282,580,581,582,585],{},"Dependabot proposes updates to every workflow action weekly, including the pinned SHAs (",[247,583,584],{},".github\u002Fdependabot.yml",").",[256,587,589],{"id":588},"source-code-analysis","Source code analysis",[261,591,592,600],{},[264,593,594],{},[267,595,596,598],{},[270,597],{},[270,599],{},[277,601,602,611,623],{},[267,603,604,608],{},[282,605,606],{},[345,607,347],{},[282,609,610],{},"CodeQL static analysis of the Java and TypeScript source.",[267,612,613,617],{},[282,614,615],{},[345,616,375],{},[282,618,619,620,622],{},"Every push to ",[247,621,381],{},", and weekly.",[267,624,625,629],{},[282,626,627],{},[345,628,393],{},[282,630,631,632,635],{},"GitHub code scanning alerts from the ",[247,633,634],{},"CodeQL"," workflow.",[239,637,639],{"id":638},"control-mapping","Control mapping",[261,641,642,657],{},[264,643,644],{},[267,645,646,648,651,654],{},[270,647,347],{},[270,649,650],{},"NIST SP 800-171 Rev 2",[270,652,653],{},"SOC 2",[270,655,656],{},"ISO\u002FIEC 27001:2022",[277,658,659,672,684,697,710],{},[267,660,661,663,666,669],{},[282,662,327],{},[282,664,665],{},"3.4.1",[282,667,668],{},"CC7.1",[282,670,671],{},"A.5.9, A.8.9",[267,673,674,676,679,681],{},[282,675,425],{},[282,677,678],{},"3.11.2",[282,680,668],{},[282,682,683],{},"A.8.8",[267,685,686,688,691,694],{},[282,687,486],{},[282,689,690],{},"3.11.3, 3.14.1",[282,692,693],{},"CC7.1, CC8.1",[282,695,696],{},"A.8.8, A.8.32",[267,698,699,701,704,707],{},[282,700,550],{},[282,702,703],{},"3.4.1, 3.14.1",[282,705,706],{},"CC8.1",[282,708,709],{},"A.8.25, A.8.28",[267,711,712,714,716,718],{},[282,713,589],{},[282,715,678],{},[282,717,668],{},[282,719,720],{},"A.8.28",{"title":722,"searchDepth":723,"depth":723,"links":724},"",2,[725,729,736],{"id":241,"depth":723,"text":25,"children":726},[727],{"id":258,"depth":728,"text":259},3,{"id":322,"depth":723,"text":323,"children":730},[731,732,733,734,735],{"id":326,"depth":728,"text":327},{"id":424,"depth":728,"text":425},{"id":485,"depth":728,"text":486},{"id":549,"depth":728,"text":550},{"id":588,"depth":728,"text":589},{"id":638,"depth":723,"text":639},"How Kinotic inventories, scans and gates the container images it publishes, and where the evidence for each control is kept.","md",null,{},{"icon":227},{"title":224,"description":737},"3FixwyRonm5i0gKGY2XUeOsvjLbuw9386XMdooPBBwM",[745,747],{"title":219,"path":220,"stem":221,"description":746,"icon":222,"children":-1},"A development environment for a few peers on one physical host, what it keeps in Azure, and how their applications move to Kinotic Cloud.",{"title":229,"path":230,"stem":231,"description":748,"icon":232,"children":-1},"Which parts of Kinotic are Enterprise Features, what running them in production requires, and how the license treats substitute implementations.",1791997980143]